SignalR Realtime Notification

The Notification Service must expose a SignalR Hub.

Create:

NotificationHub

Endpoint:

/hubs/notifications

Users connect using JWT authentication.

SignalR Group Strategy

When user connects:

extract userId from JWT
add connection to group: user_{userId}

Example:

Groups.AddToGroupAsync(connectionId, $"user_{userId}")
Send Realtime Notification

After saving a notification in database:

Send realtime message:

await hubContext
 .Clients
 .Group($"user_{userId}")
 .SendAsync("notification", notification);

Payload must match UserNotification format.

Actor Resolution

If actorType = USER:

Fetch data from User Service API.

Return:

actor: {
 id
 name
 avatar
 role: "USER"
}

If actorType = COMPANY:

Fetch data from Company Service API.

Return:

company: {
 id
 name
 avatar
 role: "COMPANY"
}

If actorType = SYSTEM:

Return no actor or company.

